fully if he does lose  quite possibly not because as johnny  said you can't trust him by the way  notice how crease looks at johnny when  he says if you  lose because he's goading him about his  second place back in 1984  something crease took very personally  second place is no place you're off  you're nothing you're lost you're a  loser this season went into chris's  backstory and we learned that as a young  man he was more like hawk miguel or tori  dealing with a rough life family  hardships and bullies  and like them he took to heart some  flawed lessons from an authority  figure modeling himself after his  captain in vietnam  adopting not just his interest in  martial arts and his cigar habit  but most damagingly his kill or be  killed shed your humanity  merciless attitude kris led his students  down that same  wrong path and decades later one of them  did the same with his own students until  he wised up  but with chris in the cobra kai driving  seat again he's perpetuating the cruel  no-mercy cycle  passing it on to a new generation this  will never be overlord so you hear me  and treating school kids like they're in  a war the fight at the school was an  embarrassment  you lost soldiers and you lost the  battle fighting his mentor in vietnam  was a seminal moment for crease becoming  the man we know today  interestingly it only happened because  he stepped in to save his army pal silva  but when their allies arrived bringing  with them the possibility that both kris  and his captain could make it out of  their battle to the death alive  crease made a choice about the kind of  man he wanted to be  in a way in the finale johnny is also  only there  fighting his mentor because of someone  else his protege miguel who's been badly  beaten by the kobrakai kids  and just as crease took over from his  captain after their fight  season four will likely bring a similar  opportunity for johnny  but back in the here and now johnny  refuses to fight his son as  unlike c